        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: enforce sandbox tool policy for loopback tools [AI]",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where sandboxed agent sessions could see gateway loopback tools that should be hidden by the configured sandbox tool policy.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe gateway loopback resolver now applies the same sandbox tool-policy layer used by the other runtime tool surfaces before exposing tools to a loopback client. The change also passes the resolved sandboxed caller context into tool construction so tool implementations keep their existing sandbox-aware behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can rely on sandbox tool allow and deny settings to apply consistently to bundled loopback tool access. Non-sandboxed main sessions in non-main sandbox mode continue to use their existing tool surface.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAI-assisted.\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/tool-resolution.test.ts src/gateway/tool-resolution.exclude.test.ts` passed locally after remote providers were unavailable: 56 tests.\n",
